    "items": [
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If only I could treat you like my brother,",
          "one who nursed at my mother’s breasts,",
          "I would find you in public and kiss you,",
          "and no one would scorn me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I would lead you, I would take you,",
          "to the house of my mother who taught me.",
          "I would give you spiced wine to drink",
          "from the juice of my pomegranate."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "May his left hand be under my head,",
          "and his right arm embrace me."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Young women of Jerusalem, I charge you,",
          "do not stir up or awaken love",
          "until the appropriate time."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Young Women"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Who is this coming up from the wilderness,",
          "leaning on the one she loves?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Woman"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I awakened you under the apricot tree.",
          "There your mother conceived you;",
          "there she conceived and gave you birth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Set me as a seal on your heart,",
          "as a seal on your arm.",
          "For love is as strong as death;",
          "jealousy is as unrelenting as Sheol.",
          "Love’s flames are fiery flames —",
          "an almighty flame!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "A huge torrent cannot extinguish love;",
          "rivers cannot sweep it away.",
          "If a man were to give all his wealth for love,",
          "it would be utterly scorned."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Brothers"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Our sister is young;",
          "she has no breasts.",
          "What will we do for our sister",
          "on the day she is spoken for?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "If she is a wall,",
          "we will build a silver barricade on her.",
          "If she is a door,",
          "we will enclose her with cedar planks."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Woman"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I am a wall",
          "and my breasts like towers.",
          "So to him I have become",
          "like one who finds peace."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Solomon owned a vineyard in Baal-hamon.",
          "He leased the vineyard to tenants.",
          "Each was to bring for his fruit",
          "one thousand pieces of silver."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I have my own vineyard. ,",
          "The one thousand are for you, Solomon,",
          "but two hundred for those who take care of its fruits."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Man"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You who dwell in the gardens,",
          "companions are listening for your voice;",
          "let me hear you!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Woman"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Run away with me, my love,",
          "and be like a gazelle",
          "or a young stag",
          "on the mountains of spices."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
